{
  "case_id": "2019-19-7",
  "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Seila Law LLC",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The structure of the CFPB is unprecedented and unconstitutional. Never before in American history has Congress given so much executive power to a single individual who does not answer to the President. By significantly limiting the President's ability to remove the CFPB's director, Congress violated the core presidential prerogatives to exercise the executive power and to take care that the laws be faithfully executed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Department of Justice",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Solicitor General contends that the Court should rewrite the Dodd-Frank Act to give the President the power to remove the director."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't see how the composition of the Bureau affects your client since your client was -- the adverse action is now attributable to someone who the President could remove at will."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Department of Justice",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As a general rule, the President has the unrestricted authority to remove principal officers. Humphrey's Executor recognizes an exception for multi-member commissions, but that shouldn't be extended to single-headed agencies for two reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: I mean in this particular context, in the -- in the context of a restriction on the President's removal power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: General, isn't it true that the Department of Justice has refused to defend the constitutionality of other federal statutes even when the President's removal power is not at issue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Text, first principles, and precedent all support the validity of the removal provision at issue here. Nonetheless, the parties are in violent agreement that the provision is unconstitutional."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Solicitor General, at page 22 of his reply brief, continues to argue that the ratification precludes any relief for the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What -- what would you say to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I think the answer to the question is yes, right? You'd DIG the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How about the EPA or Homeland Security?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I -- I -- that's when you -- you began by saying that was a narrow exception that the Solicitor General adopts. Why is that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On your -- on your definition of how we should apply the standard or water it down, is what I said, would it be enough for the President to say: I don't feel that your mind and my mind go along together on the policies or administering of the agency?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "difference if we water it down to something approaching at will? What's the difference between that and overruling Humphrey and being honest about what we're doing, Mr. Clement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, let me ask this in concrete terms. So let's say that the -- the director is appointed by a prior President and the new President says: I want to remove you because I think you are too pro-consumer and you're hurting the economy, or you are not sufficiently protecting consumer interests. Would that be permissible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now it gave that responsibility, that important responsibility to the Fed, protected by for-cause removal 100 years ago."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what do you have -- do you want to add anything on what I think is quite basic, and people disagree? On the one hand, you have people -- good walls make good neighbors, let's look for a line, multi versus single or some other line."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. House of Representatives",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you compare it to, for instance, the Fed, that has seven members who serve 14-year terms. A President who serves a four-year term is, therefore, very likely to have almost no influence over the Fed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0003-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No one defends the rationale of Humphrey's Executor distinguishing between executive functions and quasi-legislative or quasi-judicial functions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cd8221c04d4b695aae4babb79617cedb40cb7f52d4661d2d5db0834d08f9a27c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cd8221c04d4b-0003-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
